-- 2026-09-04 — Jody's cron-planetanttheatre.js still hasn't written a single
-- row (confirmed live: zero events with source ilike '%planet ant%' /
-- title ilike '%uncaged%' before this script runs). The maxDuration:60 fix
-- shipped earlier tonight is unconfirmed — Vercel Cron may simply not have
-- fired again since, or something else is still wrong; we don't have
-- Vercel log access to be sure. Jody wants "Nicolas Uncaged" (and the rest
-- of Planet Ant's calendar) live now rather than waiting on that cron to
-- sort itself out, so — same move as tonight's STD x 313.electronics post:
-- get the real data in by hand instead of waiting on the automation.
--
-- Unlike that STD post, this ISN'T going through /api/submit — that only
-- gives us a pending_review row with no external_id, city, or the venue's
-- own trust tier. Instead this is a manual one-time run of the exact same
-- transform cron-planetanttheatre.js does (stripCategoryPrefix, mapCategory,
-- parseVenue, minCostDollars, formatTime12h — all reproduced from that
-- file), pulled live from CrowdWork's public API
-- (https://www.crowdwork.com/api/v2/planetanttheatre/shows) just now: every
-- show currently posted for Ant Hall + Black Box, one row per date, 10 shows
-- / 53 rows total, including "Nicolas Uncaged 11" on 2026-09-11.
--
-- Each external_id matches EXACTLY what the cron itself would generate
-- (crowdwork-planetanttheatre-<show id>-<date>) and status is 'approved'
-- (DEFAULT_STATUS, same trust tier as cron-lagerhouse.js — Planet Ant's own
-- official box office). That means once the cron actually starts running
-- successfully, it will upsert cleanly onto these same rows (same
-- on_conflict target) instead of creating duplicates, and will pick up any
-- NEW shows Planet Ant posts after this. This is a one-time catch-up, not a
-- replacement for fixing the cron — worth checking Vercel's logs for
-- cron-planetanttheatre's next scheduled run whenever you get a chance.
--
-- Image URLs below have their CDN query-string suffix stripped (confirmed
-- live that the bare URL still loads fine — looked like a cache-busting
-- token, not an auth token).

on conflict (external_id) do update set
  title = excluded.title,
  description = excluded.description,
  category = excluded.category,
  venue_name_raw = excluded.venue_name_raw,
  venue_address_raw = excluded.venue_address_raw,
  venue_city_raw = excluded.venue_city_raw,
  start_date = excluded.start_date,
  time_display = excluded.time_display,
  note = excluded.note,
  is_free = excluded.is_free,
  price_from = excluded.price_from,
  image_url = excluded.image_url,
  ticket_url = excluded.ticket_url,
  source = excluded.source;
-- NOTE: status intentionally NOT in the update-set list, matching the
-- cron's own status-preserving upsert (an admin's approve/reject on an
-- existing row survives future runs) -- see cron-planetanttheatre.js.
